# Shared storage (optional). Without these, Stryder works fine using only
# localStorage on each device — it just won't be shared between caregivers.
#
# To link it:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com (or use an existing one).
#   2. In the SQL Editor, run:
#        create table if not exists app_data (
#          id text primary key,
#          data jsonb not null,
#          updated_at timestamptz not null default now()
#        );
#   3. Project Settings -> API. Copy the "Project URL" and the
#      "service_role" secret key (NOT the anon/public key — the service
#      role key is server-only and must never be exposed to the browser;
#      this app only ever uses it inside a server-side API route).
#
# For local development, copy this file to .env.local and fill these in.
# On Vercel, add them under Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
# The same two vars also power Health > Vaccines / vet document uploads
# (Supabase Storage) — no separate setup needed there. That bucket
# ("health-documents") is created automatically, public, the first time
# someone uploads a file — see lib/supabase.ts.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# AI Triage (optional). An "ask anything" chat module with read-only access
# to the puppy's profile and Log entries (not Training or Health) — without
# this key the /triage page just shows a "not set up yet" message.
#
#   1. Get an API key from https://platform.deepseek.com (API keys section).
#   2. Paste it below (local dev) or add it under Vercel -> Project ->
#      Settings -> Environment Variables (production).
#
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL is optional and defaults to "deepseek-chat".

DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=

# Push notifications (optional). Lets caregivers get a real iOS/Android
# notification, all driven by /api/push/cron-nudges on a timer (see step 4
# below) — nothing is pushed instantly from an in-app action:
#   - "Probably due" nudges (the same rules Today's NextNeedsCard shows)
#     go to whoever's currently on duty, since they're the one who'd act.
#   - Upcoming-event reminders go to BOTH caregivers 2 hours before any
#     event logged with a future start time (Log > + Schedule event).
# Without these env vars, the Settings > Push notifications section just
# shows "not set up yet".
#
#   1. Generate a VAPID key pair (one-time, run locally):
#        npx web-push generate-vapid-keys --json
#      Paste the two keys below. NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY is safe to
#      expose to the browser (that's what "public" means here) — but
#      VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY must stay server-only, same rule as the Supabase
#      service role key above.
#   2. VAPID_SUBJECT is a mailto: link push services use as contact info if
#      something's wrong with your usage — any address you control works.
#   3. In the Supabase SQL Editor, run:
#        create table if not exists push_subscriptions (
#          endpoint text primary key,
#          caregiver text not null,
#          subscription jsonb not null,
#          created_at timestamptz not null default now()
#        );
#        create table if not exists notified_nudges (
#          id text primary key,
#          notified_at timestamptz not null default now()
#        );
#   4. CRON_SECRET is a random string you make up (e.g. `openssl rand -hex
#      32`) that protects /api/push/cron-nudges from being triggered by
#      anyone who finds the URL. Scheduled nudge checks need something to
#      actually call that URL on a timer — Vercel's own Cron only runs
#      once/day on the free Hobby plan, so point a free service like
#      https://cron-job.org at:
#        https://<your-deployment>/api/push/cron-nudges?token=<CRON_SECRET>
#      every 15-30 minutes instead.

NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=
CRON_SECRET=
